I personally appreciate the status colors.  Specifically, I appreciate
my HP being colored.  In addition, I've enabled coloring for blessed
items green, cursed items red, and any equipped items to be a lighter
shade of gray/green/red.  That alone makes it a lot more convenient
for me, though I could probably manage without the inventory coloring
just fine, I appreciate having my HP be colored.

I think, as with all GUI-focused mods, as long as there is a way to
disable their functionality, it won't negatively affect gameplay.
Like the graphical version of nethack, which shows us things (the
entire map) that we don't particularly need enhanced (I could play
just fine with ASCII), but the enhancement can help us to better enjoy
the game without detracting from the gameplay value.  In the same way
I can't stand playing the graphical version of nethack, I can
understand people disliking status colors.  I personally have watched
people with some intense item-coloring and spell-coloring, where
things are underlined, and purple, etc, and with so much colored it
distracts me and makes it difficult for me to concentrate properly,
and so it negatively affects my gameplay experience.  But since it can
be toned down, and even disabled entirely, I am not against the status
colors entirely, I simply exercise my own preference, in the same way
other people exercise their own.

